Manage the event subscriptions of buckets: the object events (put, delete, get,
or S3 event types such as s3:ObjectCreated:Put) sent to a notification target,
optionally filtered by key prefix and suffix.

The targets are configured on the server (notify_webhook, notify_kafka, ... with
"nexoctl admin config set"); "nexoctl admin notify targets ls" prints their ARN.

Usage:
  nexoctl event [flags]
  nexoctl event [command]

Available Commands:
  add         Subscribe a notification target to the events of a bucket
  list        List the event subscriptions of a bucket
  remove      Remove event subscriptions of a bucket

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for event

Global Flags:
      --config-dir string   configuration directory (default $NEXOCTL_CONFIG_DIR or ~/.nexoctl)
      --debug               dump the HTTP requests and responses on stderr, with the secrets redacted
      --json                print JSON Lines (one object per line with a "status" member)
      --no-color            disable colors (also with the NO_COLOR environment variable)
  -q, --quiet               hide confirmations and progress (results and errors are still printed)

Use "nexoctl event [command] --help" for more information about a command.
